---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the turnaround time for an SEO audit?',
    a: 'A complete SEO audit is delivered within 7 to 10 working days from receiving access to Google Search Console, Google Analytics, and the website backend. The 30-minute walkthrough call is scheduled within 5 working days of report delivery.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What access does the audit require?',
    a: 'We require read-only access to Google Search Console, Google Analytics 4, and ideally the CMS backend. We also review the Google Business Profile listing. All access is granted via email invitation without sharing passwords.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does the paid audit differ from the free audit?',
    a: 'The free audit is an automated health check covering indexation, mobile usability, Core Web Vitals, and three quick wins. The paid audit is a comprehensive, manually conducted analysis covering technical SEO, content quality, backlink profile, local SEO, and competitor benchmarking. It is delivered as a detailed PDF with a priority action plan and a 30-minute walkthrough call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the audit include implementation of fixes?',
    a: 'The audit identifies problems and prioritises them by impact. It includes a clear action plan that can be implemented internally or handed to a development team. For organisations that require implementation, we offer ongoing SEO retainers starting from £750 per month.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the cost of an SEO audit in Birmingham?',
    a: 'Our one-off SEO audit is priced at £497. This includes the full technical, content, backlink, and local SEO analysis, a detailed PDF report, a priority action plan, and a 30-minute video walkthrough call. There are no hidden costs or ongoing commitments.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can the audit be used to brief a different agency?',
    a: 'Yes. The audit report belongs to the client and can be used in any way required. Many Birmingham organisations use it to brief their in-house team or compare recommendations from other agencies. The report is designed to be clear and actionable regardless of who implements it.',
  },
];

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'SEO Audit Birmingham',
  description: 'Comprehensive SEO audit for Birmingham businesses covering technical SEO, content analysis, backlink profile, local SEO, and competitor benchmarking.',
  provider: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Colmore SEO',
    url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk',
    sameAs: [],
    areaServed: {
      '@type': 'City',
      name: 'Birmingham',
      containedInPlace: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'West Midlands' },
    },
  },
  serviceType: 'SEO Audit',
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'City',
    name: 'Birmingham',
    containedInPlace: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'West Midlands' },
  },
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    price: '497',
    priceCurrency: 'GBP',
    availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock',
    priceValidUntil: '2026-12-31',
    description: 'One-off comprehensive SEO audit including PDF report, action plan, and 30-minute walkthrough call',
  },
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Base
  title="SEO Audit Birmingham | Colmore SEO"
  description="Comprehensive SEO audit for Birmingham businesses. Technical, content, backlink, and local SEO analysis with a prioritised action plan and walkthrough. £497."
  schema={[serviceSchema, faqSchema]}
  ogType="website"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1>SEO Audit Birmingham</h1>

    <p>An SEO audit is a systematic examination of every factor that influences a website's search engine visibility. For Birmingham businesses operating in competitive local markets, a professional audit reveals exactly why a site is underperforming and delivers a prioritised roadmap to correct it.</p>

    <div class="quick-answer">
      <strong>Quick Answer:</strong> Our Birmingham SEO audit covers technical health, content quality, backlink profile, local SEO, and competitor analysis. Deliverables include a detailed PDF report, a priority action plan ranked by impact, and a 30-minute video walkthrough call. One-off price: <strong>£497</strong>. <a href="/contact/">Request a proposal</a>.
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>Audit Scope and Methodology</h2>

      <p>Every audit follows the same rigorous methodology, applied to the specific context of each Birmingham business. We do not rely on automated reports alone. Each section is manually reviewed and annotated with specific, evidence-based recommendations.</p>

      <h3>Technical SEO Analysis</h3>
      <p>Our team crawls the entire site to identify indexation issues, broken links, redirect chains, duplicate content, slow page speeds, Core Web Vitals failures, mobile usability problems, and structured data errors. This mirrors the scope of our dedicated <a href="/technical-seo-birmingham/">technical SEO service</a>, but within the broader audit framework.</p>

      <h3>Content Quality Assessment</h3>
      <p>We evaluate every indexable page for keyword targeting, content depth, heading structure, internal linking, and topical relevance. Thin content, cannibalisation (where multiple pages compete for the same keyword), and content gaps relative to Birmingham competitors are all flagged with specific remediation steps.</p>

      <h3>Backlink Profile Review</h3>
      <p>Using Ahrefs data, we assess domain authority, referring domain quality, anchor text distribution, and toxic link risk. We benchmark the backlink profile against the top-ranking Birmingham competitors for target keywords to identify precise link-building opportunities.</p>

      <h3>Local SEO Assessment</h3>
      <p>For Birmingham businesses, local SEO is frequently the highest-ROI area. We audit Google Business Profile completeness, NAP (Name, Address, Phone) consistency across directories, local citation presence, review profile, and local pack eligibility for target queries.</p>

      <h3>Competitor Benchmarking</h3>
      <p>We identify the top 5 organic competitors in Birmingham and analyse their differentiators. This covers content strategy, technical setup, backlink sources, and local SEO presence. The output is a set of specific, actionable insights on where gaps exist and how to exploit them.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Audit Process</h2>

      <p>The audit follows a structured five-step process from initial setup to final delivery.</p>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Access and configuration.</strong> The client grants read-only access to Google Search Console and Google Analytics 4. Our team configures crawling tools and begins data collection. This takes one working day.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical crawl and data gathering.</strong> We execute a full site crawl, pull 16 months of search performance data, export the backlink profile, and audit the Google Business Profile. This runs in parallel over 2 to 3 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Manual analysis and annotation.</strong> Our team manually reviews every data point, cross-references findings, and writes specific recommendations for the business. No generic advice: every recommendation references actual pages, keywords, and Birmingham competitors. This takes 3 to 5 working days.</li>
        <li><strong>Report compilation.</strong> Findings are compiled into a structured PDF report with an executive summary, detailed section breakdowns, and a priority action plan ranked by estimated impact and implementation difficulty.</li>
        <li><strong>Walkthrough call.</strong> We schedule a 30-minute video call to present key findings, answer questions, and discuss implementation priorities. The call is recorded for distribution to internal teams or developers.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Deliverables</h2>

      <p>All audit deliverables are designed for immediate action, whether the client implements changes internally, briefs a developer, or engages us for ongoing SEO.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>PDF audit report</strong> (typically 30 to 50 pages) covering all five audit areas with screenshots, data tables, and specific recommendations</li>
        <li><strong>Priority action plan</strong> as a standalone spreadsheet, ranked by impact (high/medium/low) and effort (quick fix/medium/complex), providing a clear starting point</li>
        <li><strong>30-minute video walkthrough call</strong> with our team, recorded for reference</li>
        <li><strong>Raw data exports</strong> including crawl data, keyword rankings, and backlink profile for internal records</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>When an SEO Audit Delivers ROI</h2>

      <p>An audit is most valuable at specific inflection points. The following scenarios indicate that an audit will deliver a measurable return on investment.</p>

      <h3>New Businesses Launching in Birmingham</h3>
      <p>For any new website launching in Birmingham, an audit of the staging site before go-live prevents costly errors. We identify indexation blockers, missing redirects from legacy domains, and local SEO configuration gaps before they affect rankings.</p>

      <h3>Organisations Losing Organic Traffic</h3>
      <p>Traffic declines following Google algorithm updates signal that something requires correction. An audit pinpoints whether the cause is technical (site speed, crawl errors), content-related (thin pages, cannibalisation), or penalty-related (toxic backlinks, manual actions).</p>

      <h3>Website Redesign or Platform Migration</h3>
      <p>Migrating between CMS platforms or redesigning a site is the single most dangerous moment for SEO. A pre-migration audit ensures redirect maps are complete and no ranking equity is lost. A post-migration audit catches anything that slipped through.</p>

      <h3>Absence from Birmingham's Local Pack</h3>
      <p>If competitors appear in Google's local 3-pack and the client does not, an audit identifies the specific local ranking factors responsible. Common causes include inconsistent NAP data, incomplete Google Business Profile content, and missing local schema markup.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Birmingham-Specific Audit Considerations</h2>

      <p>Every city has a distinct competitive landscape. Our audits account for factors specific to the West Midlands market.</p>

      <h3>Colmore Business District Professional Services</h3>
      <p>Law firms, accountancies, and consultancies in the Colmore district compete intensely for high-value keywords. We benchmark each site against the top-ranking Colmore competitors, analysing content depth, schema usage, and local citation profiles to expose exploitable gaps.</p>

      <h3>Jewellery Quarter Retail and E-Commerce</h3>
      <p>Jewellery Quarter businesses typically operate product-heavy sites with complex filtering and pagination. Our audit identifies crawl budget waste, product schema opportunities, and image optimisation deficiencies that cost visibility against national jewellery retailers.</p>

      <h3>NEC and Event-Based Businesses</h3>
      <p>Businesses serving the NEC, ICC, and Birmingham's conference circuit depend on seasonal search demand. Audits of these sites focus on event schema, landing page freshness, and ensuring historical event pages are properly archived rather than returning 404 errors.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Pricing</h2>

      <p>The one-off SEO audit is priced at <strong>£497</strong> inclusive of all deliverables listed above. There is no ongoing commitment or hidden subscription.</p>

      <p>If the client proceeds with implementation, the audit cost is credited against the first month of any ongoing SEO retainer. View our full <a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">SEO pricing</a> for retainer options.</p>

      <p>For a preliminary snapshot before committing, our <a href="/free-seo-audit-birmingham/">free SEO audit</a> provides an automated health check at no cost.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">Request a Proposal</h2>
      <p>Identify exactly what is holding your site back with a comprehensive, manually reviewed SEO audit.</p>
      <a href="/contact/">Request a Proposal</a>
    </div>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{faq.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.a}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Related Services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/">SEO Birmingham</a> — full SEO services overview</li>
        <li><a href="/services/">All SEO Services</a></li>
        <li><a href="/technical-seo-birmingham/">Technical SEO Birmingham</a></li>
        <li><a href="/free-seo-audit-birmingham/">Free SEO Audit Birmingham</a> — automated health check</li>
        <li><a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">SEO Pricing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/contact/">Contact Us</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
